SUMMARY:Clay Tile Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261227T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261227T110000
UID:clay-tile-workshop-2026-12-27t11-00-00-05-00@agakhanmuseum.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.agakhanmuseum.org/uploads/2026/11
 /Clay_Paid_Workshop_Shirin_Divanbeigi27-scaled-aspect-ratio-1600-1000-scal
 ed.jpg?resize=1584%2C990&gravity
DESCRIPTION:Experiment with clay and craft your own unique tile in this ha
 nds-on workshop designed for both beginners and art enthusiasts.\n\nGuided
  by our Museum Educators\, participants will explore shaping\, designing\,
  and decorating techniques inspired by ceramic works in the Aga Khan Museu
 m’s Collections. Learn how patterns and motifs have been used for centur
 ies across the Islamic world\, and experiment with tools and textures to b
 ring your vision to life. You’ll leave with a one-of-a-kind creation tha
 t blends traditional inspiration with your own creativity.
LOCATION:Aga Khan Museum\, 77 Wynford Drive\, Toronto\, ON M3C 1K1
URL:https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/2026-holiday-clay-tile-workshop/
X-SOURCE:Aga Khan Museum
